import{_ as o,o as i,c as t,ao as a}from"./chunks/framework.BilVTWPq.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Configuring the model","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"manual/configuring_the_model.md","filePath":"manual/configuring_the_model.md","lastUpdated":null}'),r={name:"manual/configuring_the_model.md"};function c(l,e,n,s,d,h){return i(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="Configuring-the-model" tabindex="-1">Configuring the model <a class="header-anchor" href="#Configuring-the-model" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Configuring the model {#Configuring-the-model}&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Every physical process in Microclimate.jl — soil thermal properties, soil hydraulics, radiation, snow, canopy, evaporation, condensation, convergence — is a separate, swappable model type. A simulation is built by choosing one implementation for each process and composing them into a <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.MicroModel"><code>MicroModel</code></a>.</p><h2 id="Composability-and-memory-management,-a-cooking-metaphor" tabindex="-1">Composability and memory management, a cooking metaphor <a class="header-anchor" href="#Composability-and-memory-management,-a-cooking-metaphor" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Composability and memory management, a cooking metaphor {#Composability-and-memory-management,-a-cooking-metaphor}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Microclimate calculations are computationally intensive and Microclimate.jl has been designed to be highly performant. Part of the performance comes from memory managemnt, reducing the need for repeated memory allocations. <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#CommonSolve.init-Tuple{MicroProblem}"><code>init</code></a> builds a <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.MicroCache"><code>MicroCache</code></a> once: it allocates every buffer the solve loop touches — soil ODE workspace, snow scratch, canopy buffers, the solar radiation output — sized for the chosen model.</p><p>A useful metaphor is setting up a kitchen for cooking cakes. The mixing bowls, oven, pans, to hold the required ingredients are all laid out once via the cache. <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#CommonSolve.solve!-Tuple{MicroCache}"><code>solve!</code></a> then bakes a cake of the type you requested with that tailored kitchen. <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.reinit!-Tuple{MicroCache, MicroInputs}"><code>reinit!</code></a> swaps in new <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.MicroInputs"><code>MicroInputs</code></a> — a different site, a different year of weather — and bakes another cake without resetting up the kitchen:</p><div class="language-julia vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">julia</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">cache </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> init</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(problem)</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">out1 </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> solve!</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(cache)          </span><span style="--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D;"># first cake</span></span>\n<span class="line"></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">reinit!</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(cache, other_inputs)</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">out2 </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> solve!</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(cache)          </span><span style="--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D;"># same kitchen, different cake</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Changing the <em>model</em> — say, swapping <code>snow_model = NoSnow()</code> for <code>SnowModel(...)</code> (frosting!), or <code>soil_hydraulic_model</code> for a different infiltration algorithm — changes what buffers are needed, so that goes through a fresh <code>MicroProblem</code>/<code>init</code>, not <code>reinit!</code>.</p><h2 id="Why-compositional" tabindex="-1">Why compositional <a class="header-anchor" href="#Why-compositional" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Why compositional {#Why-compositional}&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>MicroModel</code> is deliberately compositional: each physical process is a type implementing a small interface (an <code>Abstract*Model</code> supertype and a handful of methods), and swapping one out is a single keyword argument. This is meant to let the package grow — a new snow-density formula, a new infiltration algorithm, a new leaf-temperature solver is a new type implementing the existing interface, not a rewrite. It also makes model <em>choices</em> cheap to interrogate: because Julia&#39;s multiple dispatch selects behaviour from the argument types rather than from branches inside one function, comparing &quot;what changes if I use <code>MatricFluxPotentialAlgorithm</code> instead of <code>MatricPotentialAlgorithm</code>&quot; or &quot;what does <code>KTheoryAirProfile</code> predict versus <code>RaupachLTheoryAirProfile</code>&quot; is a one-line change to a <code>MicroModel</code>/<code>MicroConfig</code>, not a fork of the simulation. <a href="./../tutorials/soil_hydraulics_algorithms">Soil hydraulics algorithms</a> demonstrates exactly this kind of comparison.</p><h2 id="MicroModel" tabindex="-1"><code>MicroModel</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#MicroModel" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;`MicroModel` {#MicroModel}&quot;">​</a></h2><p><a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.MicroModel"><code>MicroModel</code></a> is the constant-across-runs description of the simulation: the site, and one model per part of the system, each holding its own sub-models. Not all slots have alternatives at present but the idea is to allow a community of developers to build new functionality over time where needed.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;">Slot</th><th style="text-align:left;">Holds</th><th style="text-align:left;">Default</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>hours</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">hours of the day solved</td><td style="text-align:left;">0–23</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>site</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.Site"><code>Site</code></a>: location, terrain, albedo, roughness</td><td style="text-align:left;">— (required)</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>soil</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.SoilModel"><code>SoilModel</code></a>: <code>depths</code>, <code>profile</code>, <code>properties_model</code>, <code>hydraulic_model</code>, <code>energy_model</code>, <code>moisture_strategy</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">— (required)</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>surface</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.SurfaceModel"><code>SurfaceModel</code></a>: <code>evaporation_model</code>, <code>condensation_model</code>, <code>max_surface_pool</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>SurfaceModel()</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>atmosphere</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.AtmosphereModel"><code>AtmosphereModel</code></a>: <code>heights</code>, <code>radiation</code>, <code>boundary_layer_model</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>AtmosphereModel()</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>snow</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.NoSnow"><code>NoSnow</code></a> or <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.SnowModel"><code>SnowModel</code></a></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>NoSnow()</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>canopy</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.NoCanopy"><code>NoCanopy</code></a> or <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.MultilayerCanopy"><code>MultilayerCanopy</code></a></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>NoCanopy()</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>vapour_pressure_equation</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>GoffGratch</code>, <code>Teten</code> or <code>Huang</code> (from FluidProperties.jl)</td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>GoffGratch()</code></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><code>config</code></td><td style="text-align:left;"><a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.MicroConfig"><code>MicroConfig</code></a>: iteration and data delivery</td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>MicroConfig()</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p>The soil&#39;s <code>properties_model</code> (<a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.CampbelldeVriesSoilProperties"><code>CampbelldeVriesSoilProperties</code></a>) and <code>hydraulic_model</code> (<a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.CampbellSoilHydraulics"><code>CampbellSoilHydraulics</code></a>) are required; its <code>energy_model</code> defaults to <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.SoilHeatTransport1D"><code>SoilHeatTransport1D</code></a> and its <code>moisture_strategy</code> to <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.PrescribedSoilMoisture"><code>PrescribedSoilMoisture</code></a> (from <code>environment_daily</code>), with <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.DynamicSoilMoisture"><code>DynamicSoilMoisture</code></a> solving it from rainfall. The surface&#39;s <code>condensation_model</code> defaults to <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.GarrattSegalCondensation"><code>GarrattSegalCondensation</code></a>, with <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.BulkTransferCondensation"><code>BulkTransferCondensation</code></a> and <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.NoCondensation"><code>NoCondensation</code></a> as alternatives. <code>radiation</code>&#39;s own three slots (<code>solar_radiation_model</code>, <code>longwave_model</code>, <code>shortwave_model</code>) are documented in <a href="./radiation">Radiation</a>, and the canopy&#39;s in <a href="./canopy">Canopy</a>.</p><h2 id="MicroConfig" tabindex="-1"><code>MicroConfig</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#MicroConfig" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;`MicroConfig` {#MicroConfig}&quot;">​</a></h2><p><a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.MicroConfig"><code>MicroConfig</code></a> is the &quot;how to iterate, how data is delivered&quot; side of the model, separate from the physical-process choices above:</p><ul><li><p><code>convergence</code> — a reusable <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.FixedIterationConvergence"><code>FixedIterationConvergence</code></a>/ <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.IterationToleranceConvergence"><code>IterationToleranceConvergence</code></a> strategy. How much it actually controls depends on <code>MicroProblem.time_mode</code>: for <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.NonConsecutiveDayMode"><code>NonConsecutiveDayMode</code></a> (the default) it&#39;s ignored — that mode&#39;s own <code>iterations_per_day</code> field sets the per-day iteration count instead; for <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.ConsecutiveDayMode"><code>ConsecutiveDayMode</code></a> it only applies on day 1, and only if <code>spinup_first_day=true</code>.</p></li><li><p><code>rainfall_schedule</code> — <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.DailyRainfall"><code>DailyRainfall</code></a> or <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.HourlyRainfall"><code>HourlyRainfall</code></a></p></li><li><p><code>canopy_soil_convergence</code> — how the canopy and soil-heat ODE are coupled each hour: <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.IterationToleranceConvergence"><code>IterationToleranceConvergence</code></a> (the default) iterates them to agreement; <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.SurfaceNodePrediction"><code>SurfaceNodePrediction</code></a> integrates the soil once per hour (see <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/manual/canopy#Solving-each-hour">Canopy</a>)</p></li><li><p><code>canopy_soil_relaxation</code> — under-relaxation of the iterated coupling</p></li></ul><h2 id="How-the-pieces-fit-together-each-hour" tabindex="-1">How the pieces fit together each hour <a class="header-anchor" href="#How-the-pieces-fit-together-each-hour" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How the pieces fit together each hour {#How-the-pieces-fit-together-each-hour}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The physical processes above are not all solved as one monolithic coupled system but with different aspects converging in different ways via different algorithsm:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Soil temperature</strong> is an ODE system (<a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.SoilHeatTransport1D"><code>SoilHeatTransport1D</code></a>, handed to a SciML integrator) — continuous within the hour, not a single explicit step.</p></li><li><p><strong>Canopy</strong>, when present, is jointly converged against that same ODE each hour. With <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.IterationToleranceConvergence"><code>IterationToleranceConvergence</code></a> the canopy-soil iteration repeatedly (a) solves the canopy&#39;s shortwave, longwave, wind and leaf-temperature state (with the canopy&#39;s <code>convergence_model</code>) for the current guess of ground temperature, (b) feeds the resulting ground-surface boundary condition into the soil ODE and advances it through the hour, (c) compares the new ground temperature to the previous guess, and repeats until <code>canopy_soil_convergence</code> is satisfied (or its iteration limit is hit). <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.SurfaceNodePrediction"><code>SurfaceNodePrediction</code></a> instead predicts the surface temperature between canopy solves and integrates the ODE once. Either way, canopy and soil <em>temperature</em> reach a mutually consistent state each hour.</p></li><li><p><strong>Soil moisture</strong>, ground dew/frost, and snow growth/melt are then computed once per hour, downstream of that hour&#39;s already-converged temperature — not solved simultaneously with it. Soil moisture in particular assumes the current hour&#39;s temperature as given, rather than being part of the same implicit system; the <em>next</em> hour&#39;s temperature ODE then reads back the moisture-dependent soil thermal properties (<a href="./soil_thermal_properties">Soil thermal properties</a>), so temperature and moisture are coupled at the hourly cadence, just not simultaneously within it.</p></li></ul><h2 id="MicroInputs-and-MicroProblem" tabindex="-1"><code>MicroInputs</code> and <code>MicroProblem</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#MicroInputs-and-MicroProblem" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;`MicroInputs` and `MicroProblem` {#MicroInputs-and-MicroProblem}&quot;">​</a></h2><p><a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.MicroInputs"><code>MicroInputs</code></a> is the per-run data: <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.Site"><code>Site</code></a>, <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.SoilProfile"><code>SoilProfile</code></a>, environment forcings and initial conditions. <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.MicroProblem"><code>MicroProblem</code></a> pairs a <code>MicroModel</code> with a <code>MicroInputs</code>, the days to simulate, and a <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.AbstractTimeMode"><code>AbstractTimeMode</code></a> (<a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.NonConsecutiveDayMode"><code>NonConsecutiveDayMode</code></a> for independent representative days, <a href="/Microclimate.jl/previews/PR147/api#Microclimate.ConsecutiveDayMode"><code>ConsecutiveDayMode</code></a> for a continuous run where state carries from day to day).</p><h2 id="References" tabindex="-1">References <a class="header-anchor" href="#References" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;References {#References}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>See the <a href="./references">References</a> page for the full bibliography.</p>',23)])])}const u=o(r,[["render",c]]);export{m as __pageData,u as default};
